{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le13ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le13ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "As I've been thinking about how I can be the change I want to see in the world, it is becoming clearer how much waste and pollution negatively affect our world. We produce so much waste! Where does all that garbage go? I realized I have to learn more about zero waste. It's a way of thinking that encourages manufacturers to redesign products so that they can be reused. We must think more about this. If we don't change the way we deal with waste, we will destroy the planet.</p>", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "The zero waste concept recommends a process that mirrors nature in the way that resources are reused. It's an ethical, cost-effective way to get people to change the way they live and consume to emulate sustainable natural cycles. In a sustainable cycle, objects must be designed so that discarded materials can also be used. Zero waste initiatives say that we must eliminate all discharges into the land, water or air - especially those that threaten humans, and the planet flora and fauna. Getting rid of waste right from the start means that industries and governments have to be heavily involved. Governments must write and implement policy and provide subsidies for industries to support them in their efforts to reduce waste.</p>", "id": 2, "time": "25500"}, {"image": "engenn11le13ob06re2img03.jpg", "text": "If industries have financial motivation and contributions, they will be able to focus on packaging designs, the way things are manufactured and what materials are selected to reduce waste. Zero waste also supports finding ways to eliminate waste other than using landfills or incineration and raising community awareness. If people are more aware of the possibilities for reusing waste to reduce pollution, they will put pressure on their governments to enforce zero waste initiatives. I had to learn the three Rs in school: reduce, reuse, recycle. Zero waste adds one more R: recovery. We will always have waste but we can find new ways to process it. I think if we all work together, we can really make a difference!", "id": 3, "time": "66000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about social issues, beliefs, opinions and moral or personal dilemmas.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express compulsory action.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What do you know about waste management in your city?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What more can we do to reduce waste?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Where does all that garbage go?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Zero waste is a crucial <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">initiative</span>.", "type": "text"}]