at will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Must, Have to, Had to for What is Compulsory", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to talk about what is mandatory or required, you can use the modals <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">had to</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> and <span class=\"strong\">has/have to</span> to talk about what is compulsory in the present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">All travelers to the United States <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> have proper identification.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">All changes in the law <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be passed by a majority.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about something that was necessary or obligatory in the past, you use <span class=\"strong\">had to</span>. You do not use <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, as it has another meaning when used to talk about past situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">When I lived in Japan, I <span class=\"strong\">had to</span> sort my garbage very carefully.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I realized I have to learn more about zero waste.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We must think more about this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In a sustainable cycle, objects must be designed so that discarded materials can also be used.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Zero waste initiatives say that we must eliminate all discharges into the land, water or air - especially those that threaten humans, and the planet flora and fauna.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Governments must write and implement policy and provide subsidies for industries to support them in their efforts to reduce waste.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had to learn the three Rs in school: reduce, reuse, recycle.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "First Conditional: If and If not ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> first conditional</span> to talk about real or possible situations. When you present the condition, it is common to use <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span>is usually If+present simple (If clause) and will+infinitive (result clause). <br>Remember to use a comma (,) if the If clause is at the beginning of the sentence.<br> For example: <span class=\"italic\">If we don't change the way we deal with waste<span class=\"strong\">, </span>we will destroy the planet.</span><br> <br> You can use other phrases instead of <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">if not</span> to make your language more varied and sophisticated. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Two alternatives you can use to introduce the condition clause are: <span class=\"italic\">provided that</span> and<span class=\"italic\"> so long as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span> you come down from the tree now, I won't call the fire department.<br/> = <span class=\"strong\">So long as</span> you come down from the tree now, I won't call the fire department. <br/>= <span class=\"strong\">Provided that</span> you come down from the tree now, I won't call the fire department.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Provided that</span> is more formal than <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If industries have financial motivation and contributions, they will be able to focus on packaging designs, the way things are manufactured and what materials are selected to reduce waste.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If people are more aware of the possibilities for reusing waste to reduce pollution, they will put pressure on their governments to enforce zero waste initiatives.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think if we all work together, we can really make a difference!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "waste ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unwanted material", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We produce so much waste! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about social issues.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ethical ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to moral principles", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It's an ethical, cost-effective way to get people to change the way they live and consume to emulate sustainable natural cycles. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to emulate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to match; to surpass", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We emulate people whom we admire.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sustainable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to be maintained", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to find sustainable alternatives.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "discarded ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "thrown away", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Objects must be designed so that discarded materials can also be used.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "discharge ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "substance allowed to go into the air, water or land", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Zero waste initiatives say that we must eliminate all discharges into the land, water or air - especially those that threaten humans, and the planet's flora and fauna.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, come up with an idea for improving the environment in your city or country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Develop an initiative plan. What will you do? Who will do it?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How will you do it?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a poster for your plan. Include pictures if possible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your poster and plan to your group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to the other presentations and as a group, choose the plan that you think is best.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write an initiative plan with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a poster to demonstrate my plan.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my initiative plan to a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I help decide on the best plan of the group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}]}